[handwritten note, found tucked into the research archive, not a formal document]

If you're reading this because you went looking for the workstation from batch 3's
notes -- it isn't on the compound network diagram on purpose. I set it up off the main
listing after the second consent-waiver review flagged how much of batch 3's data was
being duplicated onto the shared drive where anyone with Sound Council access could see
it. Lord Orochimaru didn't say to hide it. He also didn't say not to, and I'd rather
explain a locked door than an open one.

It's still on the compound's own segment, still reachable if you know where to look --
I'm not an idiot, I'm not taking it fully dark, that would raise more questions than it
answers if anyone came looking for a "missing" asset. It's just not on the list anyone
reads without asking first. Same practice as the curse-mark subject logs -- keep the
sensitive work one step removed from casual access, not off the grid entirely.

If Kabuto asks, tell him to ask me directly, not go digging. He already knows more about
batch 3 than the paperwork does anyway.

-- destroy after reading, or at least don't leave it where the Sound Five can find it and
make it into a joke
